        "s14": {
          "type": "policy_section",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "14. Governing Law and Jurisdiction",
            "content": "<p>These Terms of Service and any disputes or claims arising out of or in connection with them (including non-contractual disputes or claims) are governed by and construed in accordance with the <strong>laws of the Republic of India</strong>.</p><p><strong>Jurisdiction:</strong> Subject to the consumer rights exception below, any dispute arising under or in connection with these Terms shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts in <strong>[Your City], India</strong>.</p><p><strong>Dispute Resolution Process:</strong> Before initiating legal proceedings, both parties agree to first attempt to resolve any dispute in good faith through direct negotiation. Either party may notify the other of the dispute in writing, and both parties agree to engage in good-faith discussions for a period of at least <strong>30 days</strong> to attempt resolution. If the dispute remains unresolved after 30 days, either party may pursue their legal remedies.</p><p><strong>IMPORTANT \u2014 Consumer Commission Rights Preserved:</strong> Nothing in this clause prevents you, as a consumer, from approaching the <strong>District Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission</strong> in <strong>your own jurisdiction</strong> (the place where you reside or where the cause of action arises) under the Consumer Protection Act, 2019. Consumer Commissions have overriding jurisdiction in consumer disputes and cannot be restricted by contractual jurisdiction clauses. This right is non-waivable and is fully preserved.</p>"
